		{"id":"19289d2ec36465f4","type":"text","text":"Version Skew Support Policy","x":-1682,"y":-1136,"width":282,"height":50},
		{"id":"dc5105ebbc1227f8","type":"text","text":"Certificates","x":-708,"y":-1468,"width":155,"height":50},
		{"id":"53a89e5b8502b8c0","type":"text","text":"Kubeconfig","x":-732,"y":-1384,"width":155,"height":50},
		{"id":"d054380a421c9271","type":"text","text":"Flags","x":-786,"y":-1278,"width":108,"height":50},
		{"id":"eb4576e18608faba","type":"text","text":" the newest and oldest kube-apiserver instances must be within one minor version.","x":-2809,"y":-1328,"width":694,"height":50},
		{"id":"e7c479b288d7b8c6","type":"text","text":"kubelet must not be newer than kube-apiserver, and may be up to two minor versions older.","x":-2874,"y":-1256,"width":759,"height":50},
		{"id":"f09edc9b3424a100","type":"text","text":"kube-apiserver","x":-2032,"y":-1328,"width":183,"height":50},
		{"id":"0f6549429533ac3f","type":"text","text":"- kube-controller-manager\n- kube-scheduler\n- cloud-controller-manager","x":-2142,"y":-1163,"width":293,"height":106},
		{"id":"9c9428c41ade5edf","type":"text","text":"kubectl is supported within one minor version (older or newer) of kube-apiserver.","x":-2718,"y":-1032,"width":681,"height":50},
		{"id":"cff64d3db281ed81","type":"text","text":"Must not be newer than the kube-apiserver.\nExpected to match the kube-apiserver minor version. \nCan be upto one minor version older","x":-2738,"y":-1163,"width":488,"height":105},
		{"id":"fc986ca8ae2a313f","type":"text","text":"Setup K8S from scratch","x":-1337,"y":-1253,"width":246,"height":50},
		{"id":"fc7656d0820bb0c5","type":"text","text":"Security","x":-2713,"y":3022,"width":130,"height":50},
		{"id":"7eb3aab0f3e2e59d","type":"text","text":"Taint & Toleration","x":-2560,"y":3369,"width":198,"height":50},
		{"id":"8e4f95878ca53eda","type":"text","text":"- Taints allow a node to repel a set of pods.\n- Tolerations allow the scheduler to schedule pods with matching taints.","x":-2267,"y":3320,"width":639,"height":74},
		{"id":"619e3d4314ae0771","type":"text","text":"-  Checks if the **application has started successfully**\n-  delays liveness and readiness probes as it checks if the container started correctly then liveness and readiness check the capability of  the container to serve requests\n-  action: restart","x":-2601,"y":900,"width":641,"height":157},
		{"id":"8d4f184c6035888d","type":"text","text":"- Checks if the **container is still alive** -> sends http request to the pod\n-  action: restart","x":-2521,"y":689,"width":561,"height":60},
		{"id":"aa90bbc7d5e989b8","type":"text","text":"- Checks if the **container is ready to serve traffic** (latency test)\n- action: get out of service","x":-2475,"y":792,"width":515,"height":82},
		{"id":"d93b97ab0e55a00e","type":"text","text":"Probes","x":-1520,"y":834,"width":95,"height":50},
		{"id":"e0f37f56238c7db0","type":"text","text":"**Liveness Probe**","x":-1916,"y":689,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b5ff95523a414db1","type":"text","text":"**Readiness Probe**","x":-1916,"y":803,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d0c04debccafa29f","type":"text","text":"Startup Probe","x":-1916,"y":948,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5e11420bf9d94f4c","type":"text","text":"scheduling","x":-2817,"y":3419,"width":148,"height":50},
		{"id":"12ebbf7bcc5f1fcc","type":"text","text":"```\nkubectl taint nodes node1 key1=value1:effect\n```","x":-2267,"y":3444,"width":639,"height":78},
		{"id":"db5f245014fc11e8","type":"text","text":"Service Account","x":-2457,"y":2910,"width":190,"height":50},
		{"id":"4d99feaedf530524","type":"text","text":" Store data that is used for SSH authentication. ","x":-2432,"y":1625,"width":379,"height":50},
		{"id":"acb97dac40889e30","type":"text","text":" Store a certificate and a key that are used for TLS. ","x":-2525,"y":1707,"width":430,"height":50},
		{"id":"5c01d2531a99b389","type":"text","text":" Store the credentials for accessing a container image registry.","x":-2694,"y":1790,"width":516,"height":50},
		{"id":"a648e03650b4a10c","type":"text","text":"Docker configuration secrets","x":-2103,"y":1790,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"0592aa1d8dc53ac9","type":"text","text":" Basic authentication secrets","x":-2114,"y":1536,"width":263,"height":50},
		{"id":"1f42a7ce8a46526e","type":"text","text":"Pods can consume ConfigMaps as environment variables, command-line arguments, or as configuration files in a volume.","x":-2571,"y":1192,"width":917,"height":50},
		{"id":"f19f5c4ceb581a4f","type":"text","text":"A Secret is an object that contains a small amount of sensitive data such as a password, a token, or a key.","x":-2432,"y":1285,"width":810,"height":50},
		{"id":"3f6f96de02bd41a1","type":"text","text":"","x":-2242,"y":1126,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"97bd6ab41d68d863","type":"text","text":" Store a token credential for applications that authenticate to the Kubernetes API.","x":-2752,"y":1456,"width":618,"height":50},
		{"id":"31896d79251f685b","type":"text","text":" is an API object used to store non-confidential data in key-value pairs.","x":-2217,"y":1107,"width":563,"height":50},
		{"id":"af126f8a1143a220","type":"text","text":"The namespace for objects created by the Kubernetes system","x":-2240,"y":-169,"width":554,"height":50},
		{"id":"aa3bee13e9225ce8","type":"text","text":"- This namespace is readable by _all_ clients (including those not authenticated).\n- This namespace is mostly reserved for cluster usage, in case that some resources should be visible and readable publicly throughout the whole cluster.","x":-2913,"y":-77,"width":1245,"height":80},
		{"id":"536c09e467fcae5f","type":"text","text":"Node leases allow the kubelet to send heartbeats so that the control plane can detect node failure.","x":-2574,"y":51,"width":827,"height":50},
		{"id":"db9a4e5474e37455","type":"text","text":"Used for resources with no specific namespace.","x":-2100,"y":-256,"width":429,"height":50},
		{"id":"f8be97daa0695bc6","type":"text","text":"Ingress","x":1565,"y":-97,"width":136,"height":50},
